$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM M2. L1H2 (3.58 g, 0.01 mol), diethyleneglygol (0.948 ml, 0.01 mol),
dicyclohexyl-carbodilimide (DCC) (4.12 g, 0.02 mol) and a small amount of
DMAP were used to prepare M2 as per this procedure. The product was
purified through column chromatography filled with silica gel as the
stationary phase and acetonitrile as the mobile phase as described
previously. Yield (60%). Elemantal analysis (%) calcd. for C22H21O9:
calc. (found) C, 61.54 (61.42); H, 4.93 (4.81). ES-MS: calc. for C22H21O9
(M+1)+, 429; found: 429.01. 1H NMR (CDCl3, δ, TMS, 500.13 MHz):
7.756-7.736 (m, ar, 2H), 7.723-7.705 (m, 2H), 7.558-7.516 (m, 4H), 4.613
(-CH2,4H), 4.483-4.466 (-CH2,4H), 3.801-3.784 (-CH2,4H). 13C NMR (CDCl3,
δ, TMS, 125.75 MHz): 167.934 (C=O), 167.174 (C=O), 132.198 (quat-C),
131.420, 131.307, 131.138, 129.274, 129.110 (=CH-aromatic), 68.896
(-CH2), 65.107 (-CH2), 62.772 (-CH2). IR spectra: (ʋ, cm_1) ʋ COO=3038,
2929, 2852, 1731, 1626, 1576, 1443, 1281, 1117, 1047, 743.
