$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.3.2. Synthesis of Mono-ols. To a solution of
1 mmol monoacid and 1.2 mmol diol (2, 3-dihydroxypropyl oleate) in 6 mL
of CHCl3 under the protection of N2, 0.2 mmol DMAP was added, followed by
1.2 mmol DCC. The reaction was carried out at room temperature overnight.
The precipitated dicyclohexylurea was removed by filtration. The organic
phase was diluted with 10 mL of chloroform then washed sequentially with
water (3 x 20 mL), 4% aqueous NaHCO3 (2 x 200 mL), and brine (3 x 200
mL), and then dried over Na2SO4. After filtration, the filtrate was
concentrated with a rotary evaporator and the residue was purified by
column chromatography with ethyl acetate and hexanes as the eluent. From
mono acid 2 and 2,3-dihydroxypropyl oleate. From mono acid 3 and
2,3-dihydroxypropyl oleate. Mono-ol 3, yield 60%. 1H-NMR (in CDCl3, δ/
ppm): 5.35-5.21(20H, m), 4.31-4.22 (6H, dd), 4.12-4.07 (10H, dd),
2.30-2.24 (22H, m), 2.02-1.93 (32H, m), 1.60-1.55 (22H, m), 1.28-1.22
(148H,m), 0.88-0.84 (15H, t).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, acid reactant concentration dependent product formation,
Steglich esterification
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Physical Properties of Triacylglycerol Oligomers: Examining
the Physical Functionality Potential of Self-Metathesized Highly
Unsaturated Vegetable Oils
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Li, Shaojun; Bouzidi, Laziz; Narine, Suresh S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research (2013), 52(6), 2209-2219

