$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Ethyl 2,4-Dihydroxybenzoate (II). 2,4-Dihydroxybenzoic acid
(8.00 g, 51.90 mmol) was dissolved in 40 ml of ethanol (31.56 g, 686.08
mmol). The solution was heated to 60 °C under stirring condition.
Concentrated sulfuric acid (3 ml) was dropwise added to the reaction
vessel in 30 minutes. Then the reaction mixture was refluxed for 12 h.
After cooling, the pH of the solution was adjusted to 5-6 with the
aqueous solution of sodium bicarbonate. After extracted with ether and
distilled under reduced pressure, crystals were obtained. White crystals
(5.24 g, 55.4%). FT-IR [KBr, cm-1]: 3500, 2960, 2930, 2870, 2850, 1650,
1450, 1280, 1150, 1086, 830, 794, 764, 718.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
