$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.4. Synthesis of Oligomers. 3.4.1. Synthesis
of Oligomers with Odd Numbers (Procedure A). To a solution of 2 mmol
monoacids and 1 mmol diol (2,3-dihydroxypropyl oleate) in 10 mL of CHCl3
under the protection of N2, 0.4 mmol DMAP was added, followed by 2.2 mmol
DCC. The reaction was carried out at room temperature overnight. The
precipitated dicyclohexylurea was removed by filtration. The organic
phase was diluted with 10 mL of chloroform, then washed sequentially with
water (3 x 20 mL), 4% aqueous NaHCO3 (2 x 200 mL), and brine (3 x 200
mL), and then dried over Na2SO4. After filtration, the filtrate was
concentrated with a rotary-evaporator and the residue was purified by
column chromatography with ethyl acetate and hexanes as the eluent. From
monoacid 1 and 2,3-dihydroxypropyl oleate following procedure A. From
monoacid 2 and 2,3-dihydroxypropyl oleate following procedure A.
Pentamer, yield 35%. 1H-NMR (in CDCl3, δ/ ppm): 5.36-5.30 (22H, m),
5.25-5.23 (5H, m), 4.29-4.24 (10H,dd), 4.14-4.10 (10H, dd), 2.30-2.26
(30H, t), 1.99-1.93 (44H, m), 1.59 (30H, br), 1.28-1.24 (204H, m),
0.88-0.84 (21H, t). 13C-NMR (in CDCl3, δ/ppm): 173.47, 173.06, 130.52,
130.23, 129.93, 69.09, 62.31, 34.41, 34.25, 32.81, 32.13, 29.99-29.28,
27.44, 27.39, 25.11, 25.06, 22.90, 14.33. MS: 3434 [M+NH4]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM acid reactant concentration dependent product formation, Steglich
esterification
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Physical Properties of Triacylglycerol Oligomers: Examining
the Physical Functionality Potential of Self-Metathesized Highly
Unsaturated Vegetable Oils
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
