$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2.3.2. Synthesis of the Base Diester (E)-Didec-9-enyl Octadec-9-enedioate
(H). To a solution of 1,18-octadec-9-enedioic acid (15.6 g, 50 mmol) and
9-decen-1-ol (23.4 g, 150 mmol) in CHCl3 (100 mL) at ∼0 °C, was added
DMAP (12.2 g, 100 mmol), followed by slow addition of DCC (22.7 g, 110
mmol). The reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature and
kept overnight. The mixture was filtered to remove the solid. The
filtrate was concentrated with a rotary evaporator. The residue was
purified by flash chromatography using hexanes:ethyl acetate (40:1).
Colorless oil, yield 28 g. 1H-NMR in CDCl3: 5.83-5.78 (2H, m), 5.36-5.34
(2H, t), 4.99-4.89 (4H, dd), 4.05-4.01 (4, t), 2.28-2.24 (4H, t),
2.04-1.99 (4H, m), 1.94-1.92 (4H, m), 1.61-1.57 (8H, m), 1.4-1.2 (36, m).
